# VeloxPOS — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
#
# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. NOTE (verified against Prisma 6.x):
#   • The RUNTIME (next dev / next build / standalone server) reads THIS
#     value; src/lib/db-path.ts re-resolves a relative `file:` URL against
#     the repo that owns prisma/schema.prisma, so `file:../db/custom.db`
#     always lands at <repo>/db/custom.db regardless of the process CWD.
#   • The Prisma CLI anchors SHELL-provided relative URLs against
#     prisma/schema.prisma (verified) but .env-loaded ones against the CWD —
#     so the `db:*` npm scripts set DATABASE_URL inline (shell-provided,
#     schema-anchored) instead of relying on .env auto-loading.
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" + a postgresql url in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/veloxpos

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — used for metadata, sitemap.xml, and robots.txt.
# Set to the deployed URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth.
# REQUIRED in production — ENFORCED AT BOOT (session-22): the production
# server refuses to start without a real secret (missing/empty/the public
# dev fallback → the process exits with an actionable message pointing
# here); dev/test fall back to an insecure local constant with a boot
# warning. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32` (64 hex chars — secrets
# shorter than 32 chars boot with a weak-key warning).
AUTH_SECRET=""
